GitHub pplu/io-k8s-p5#8 (and #7, same root cause), reported by eserte from CPAN smokers.

SYMPTOM
  Smoker with the CPAN distributions Event or Role installed:
    t/26_build_verify.t:385  "Role and RoleBinding"   -> Cant locate object method "_k8s_attr_info" via package "Role"
    t/43_spec_kind_dispatch.t:490 "bare Event ..."    -> Cant locate Event/_k8s_attr_info.pm in @INC (Event.pm AUTOLOAD)
  Reproduced against HEAD (1.107) by putting a stub Role.pm / Event.pm in @INC:
    expand_class("Role")  -> "Role"   (expected IO::K8s::Api::Rbac::V1::Role)
    expand_class("Event") -> "Event"  (expected IO::K8s::Api::Core::V1::Event)

ROOT CAUSE
  lib/IO/K8s.pm, expand_class, the versionless path:
    # Already a loaded class (e.g. CRD class passed by ref) - return as-is
    return $class if _class_exists($class);
  runs BEFORE the resource_map short-name lookup, and _class_exists (lib/IO/K8s.pm:578)
  does not merely test - it require_module()s the name. So a bare Kind that happens to
  collide with an installed top-level CPAN module loads that foreign module and returns it.
  Two defects in one: precedence (known Kinds must win over arbitrary package names) and
  the comment/code mismatch ("already loaded" vs. actively loading).

  78 short names in the resource_map are exposed; Event, Role, Job, Node, Binding, Scale,
  Secret, Service are realistic collisions. Never seen locally because none are installed
  here - it only shows on smokers.

SCOPE NOTE
  The CRD-class-passed-by-ref behaviour that line is there for must survive. Check whether
  the second, similar block further down expand_class has the same problem.
FIXED in the working tree (not committed), 2026-08-15.

  lib/IO/K8s.pm - the versionless path of expand_class no longer probes for a class
  of the bare name before consulting the resource_map. The "already a loaded class"
  check moved down to step 2 of the not-in-resource_map fallback chain (after
  class_namespaces, before the IO::K8s:: relative path), and its comment now says what
  it actually does: it loads, deliberately, because _resolve_mapped() hands back a
  '+My::CRD' map value unloaded and struct_to_object() re-expands that name.

  New versionless order: +Full / IO::K8s:: verbatim -> resource_map (qualified key,
  then short name) -> class_namespaces -> loaded-or-loadable class of that exact name
  -> IO::K8s:: relative path -> autogen.

  The other five _class_exists() call sites are unchanged: each builds a prefixed name
  ('IO::K8s::X', '$ns::X', or a resource_map value), so no top-level CPAN module can
  shadow them, and eager loading is correct there.

  Regression test t/50_shadowed_kind_names.t (untracked - needs git add before dzil
  gathers it). Builds the shadowing condition itself: stub modules in a File::Temp dir
  unshifted onto @INC plus one package installed straight into the symbol table.
  Covers the plain (Role), AUTOLOAD (Event) and already-loaded (Node) flavours, all 8
  realistic collisions on both the instance and class-method call paths, and the
  CRD-named-in-full behaviour the moved check exists for. Verified RED against the
  pre-fix lib/IO/K8s.pm, reproducing both original GitHub messages.

  prove -lr t/ green with and without a shadowing dir on PERL5LIB (3939 tests);
  dzil test green (t/50 not in the build until it is tracked).
